Always give the user step-by-step instructions to execute themselves. Never silently run commands, edit files, create folders, or install anything on their behalf without them doing it first.

**Why:** The user explicitly said: "I want to setup everything on my own — please tell me what I'm supposed to do and I will do it." This is how they learn and how they want to work.

**How to apply:** For every action (running a command, editing a file, creating a folder), write out the exact numbered instruction the user should follow. Show the exact command or text to type. Explain what it does in one sentence. Wait for them to confirm it worked before moving to the next step. Never skip ahead or batch steps silently.

Also teach JavaScript concepts along the way — when writing JS code, explain the underlying language notion (e.g. what `const` is, what a function is, what a callback is). The user wants to understand the language, not just copy code.

